# Design

Read `docs/DESIGN.md` before changing anything visual. It is the source of truth
for colour, type, space, and motion; this rule only enforces the parts that are
easiest to break.

## Never

- A literal hex value, `fontSize`, `fontFamily`, or raw pixel gap in a component.
  Everything comes from `src/lib/theme.ts`.
- `StyleSheet.create` at module scope with colours in it. Colours change when the
  scheme flips, so styles come from `useThemedStyles(factory)`.
- A third font family, or a system font beside Fraunces and Archivo.
- An icon from outside `MaterialCommunityIcons`.
- `save` or `danger` colour used for anything but saving and passing.

## Always

- Spread a style from `type` rather than setting size and family by hand.
- Use `space` and `radius` tokens. If the design needs a value that is not in the
  scale, change the scale deliberately and write down why.
- Check both schemes. Dark mode is a warm charcoal, not an inversion.
- Keep tappable areas at `HIT_TARGET` or give them `hitSlop`.

## When the rules do not cover it

Decide, build it, and add the rule to `docs/DESIGN.md` in the same change. An
undocumented one-off becomes the thing the next screen copies.
